    "final_answer": "I have found the necessary information. Let me provide the comprehensive answer about the open-source conversational AI model trained in English on Hugging Face.\n\n---\n\n## Open-Source Conversational AI Model: **Microsoft/DialoGPT-medium**\n\n**Model Page:** https://huggingface.co/microsoft/DialoGPT-medium\n\n### Overview\n**DialoGPT** is a State-of-the-Art (SOTA) large-scale pretrained dialogue response generation model for multi-turn conversations, released by Microsoft Research. It is hosted on Hugging Face under the MIT License (open-source).\n\n### Key Specifications\n| Attribute | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Base Architecture** | GPT-2 |\n| **Pipeline Tag** | Text Generation (also tagged `conversational`) |\n| **Libraries Supported** | PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX, Rust, Transformers |\n| **Training Language** | English (trained on 147M multi-turn dialogues from Reddit discussion threads) |\n| **Downloads (last month)** | 215,929 |\n| **Community Likes** | 441 |\n| **Associated Paper** | arXiv:1911.00536 (Nov 2019) – *\"DialoGPT: Large-Scale Generative Pre-training for Conversational Response Generation\"* |\n\n### Main Features\n1. **Multi-Turn Conversation Generation** – Generates contextually relevant responses across multiple conversational turns (not just single-turn replies).\n2. **Large-Scale Pretraining** – Trained on 147 million multi-turn dialogue exchanges from Reddit, giving it broad conversational coverage.\n3. **Human-Like Response Quality** – Human evaluation shows the responses are comparable in quality to those of humans under a single-turn Turing test.\n4. **GPT-2 Based Architecture** – Inherits the strong autoregressive language modeling capabilities of GPT-2.\n5. **Multiple Sizes Available** – DialoGPT is available in small, medium, and large variants.\n6. **Highly Extensible** – 35 adapters, 93 fine-tunes, and 3 quantizations have been built on top of this model by the community.\n7. **Easy Integration** – Can be loaded with `AutoModelForCausalLM` and `AutoTokenizer` from the `transformers` library in just a few lines of code.\n\n### Applications\n- **Chatbots and Virtual Assistants** – Building conversational agents for customer service or general chitchat (e.g., it is used in Microsoft's HuggingGPT Space on HF).\n- **Open-Domain Dialogue Systems** – Generating coherent responses to arbitrary conversational topics.\n- **Empathetic Response Generation** – Used in spaces like `arya7113/empathetic-response-ai` for emotionally aware replies.\n- **Research and Benchmarking** – Cited as a benchmark model for evaluating dialogue systems (referenced in leaderboards like the Intel low-bit Open LLM Leaderboard and BAAI Open Chinese LLM Leaderboard).\n- **Educational Toolkits** – Used for teaching conversational AI concepts, with 100+ Hugging Face Spaces built on top of it.\n- **Fine-Tuning Base for Custom Bots** – Provides a strong pretrained starting point for building domain-specific conversational agents.\n- **Conversational Research Prototyping** – Supports both Python (Transformers) and Rust inference, enabling rapid experimentation.\n\n### How to Use (Quick Example from Model Card)\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer\nimport torch\n\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"microsoft/DialoGPT-medium\")\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\"microsoft/DialoGPT-medium\")\n\n# Multi-turn chat loop\nfor step in range(5):\n    new_user_input_ids = tokenizer.encode(input(\">> User:\") + tokenizer.eos_token, return_tensors='pt')\n    bot_input_ids = torch.cat([chat_history_ids, new_user_input_ids], dim=-1) if step > 0 else new_user_input_ids\n    chat_history_ids = model.generate(bot_input_ids, max_length=1000, pad_token_id=tokenizer.eos_token_id)\n    print(\"DialoGPT: {}\".format(tokenizer.decode(chat_history_ids[:, bot_input_ids.shape[-1]:][0], skip_special_tokens=True)))\n```\n\n### Conclusion\n**Microsoft/DialoGPT-medium** is a strong representative example of an open-source, English-trained conversational AI model on Hugging Face. With its MIT license, extensive community adoption (215K+ monthly downloads), 100+ derivative Spaces, and a robust GPT-2 based architecture pretrained on 147M Reddit conversations, it remains a foundational model for both production chatbots and academic dialogue research.",
